    "slot_value": "Use simple labels: current, due soon, overdue, exempt, and missing. Current needs no action. Due soon should prompt a reminder. Overdue should escalate to staff follow-up and a family notice. Exempt should show that it is approved and on file. Missing should clearly mean the document has not been received yet. Incomplete, expired, or noncompliant immunization records should be flagged for staff review right away; families may upload a replacement record; the child must not be marked compliant until staff confirms the replacement meets requirements; if still unresolved after review, the child remains out of compliance and that status is visible to staff. If an immunization record is incomplete, overdue, or missing at go-live, the child should stay enrolled but be clearly marked not compliant until the record is verified or updated; staff should be able to see which items are missing and follow up with the family; if the center has a temporary-exception policy, the system should support it. For go-live data migration, if the core record is mostly complete, it should go live with whatever is valid and missing or inconsistent pieces should be flagged for cleanup afterward. If the issue affects something critical like pickup authorization, active enrollment status, or an unpaid balance that changes billing, the record should be held until verified. Conflicting data should not overwrite the source silently; it should be deferred or marked for review so staff can correct it before it becomes the official record.",
